 ts name no 2028 host. Meeting and main-paper dates are two-year proxies f
 rom ECCV 2026's 22:00 UTC cutoffs\; no annual 2027 edition is invented. T
 he timezone refers to the prior edition\, not a 2028 host.\nScope: Broad 
 research in visual perception\, representation learning\, recognition\, s
 egmentation\, 3D geometry and reconstruction\, computational imaging\, an
 d image/video synthesis. Vision-language models\, multimodal understandin
 g\, human motion and appearance\, and robust visual systems extend this c
 ore. ECCV is the biennial European flagship for computer vision\; the sco
 pe uses the actual published 2026 CFP\, not an invented 2028 call.\nAddit
 ional topics: Computer Graphics & Visualization\, Multimedia Learning & R
 etrieval\, Natural Language Processing & LLMs\, Biometrics & Human Sensin
 g\, Robustness & Safety\nScope sources (2026): https://eccv.ecva.net/Conf
